From 71c998a3e25a138a7ba4c6eea61d95d41fe3f7be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Wloga <michal.wloga@envirosolutions.pl>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:40:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] [server] Write 32 bits PNG images with libpng, without
 row filtering

WMS images in the default PNG format were written with QImage::save(), which uses the adaptive row filters of libpng and the default deflate level. For rendered maps the filters cost time and make the result larger, and the encoding took more than half of the time of a 1024x768 GetMap request.

RGB32 and ARGB32 images are now written directly with libpng, with no row filter and deflate level 2. The decoded pixels are identical to the previous output; other PNG modes (8 bits, 16 bits, 1 bit) still use the writer of Qt.

Measured with 4 FCGI workers on PostGIS layers, median of a 1024x768 GetMap with one client: 26.9 ms -> 14.0 ms (one layer) and 42.7 ms -> 24.8 ms (three layers); throughput with 16 clients +30 %; responses are 13 % smaller.

